{
  "title": "Adding and transforming columns",
  "summary": "Derived columns, conditions, mappings, bins and tidy names.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "New columns are vectorised",
      "body": [
        "Assigning to a new name adds a column, computed for every row at once:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "df[\"revenue\"] = df[\"qty\"] * df[\"price\"]",
        "df[\"vat\"] = (df[\"revenue\"] * 0.2).round(2)",
        "df[\"product\"] = df[\"product\"].str.upper()     # replace a column",
        "```",
        "",
        "`assign` does the same but returns a **new** DataFrame and leaves `df` alone, which makes it",
        "safe inside functions and easy to chain:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "out = df.assign(revenue=df[\"qty\"] * df[\"price\"])",
        "out = df.assign(revenue=lambda d: d[\"qty\"] * d[\"price\"])   # lambda sees the frame so far",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"qty\": [2, 5], \"price\": [1.5, 4.0]})",
        "out = df.assign(revenue=lambda d: d[\"qty\"] * d[\"price\"],",
        "                big=lambda d: d[\"revenue\"] > 10)",
        "print(out.columns.tolist())",
        "print(df.columns.tolist())",
        "print(out[\"revenue\"].tolist(), out[\"big\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "['qty', 'price', 'revenue', 'big']",
        "['qty', 'price']",
        "[3.0, 20.0] [False, True]"
      ],
      "explain": "`assign` returns a new frame; later keywords can use earlier ones through the lambda."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Conditions, mappings and bins",
      "body": [
        "Four tools cover most derived columns:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "df[\"size\"] = np.where(df[\"qty\"] >= 3, \"bulk\", \"single\")    # if/else per row",
        "df[\"zone\"] = df[\"region\"].map({\"North\": \"N\", \"South\": \"S\"})  # look up; unmapped -> NaN",
        "df[\"band\"] = pd.cut(df[\"price\"], bins=[0, 5, 10, 100],",
        "                    labels=[\"cheap\", \"mid\", \"premium\"])      # numeric ranges -> labels",
        "df[\"code\"] = df.apply(lambda row: row[\"product\"][:3] + row[\"region\"][0], axis=1)",
        "```",
        "",
        "`apply(..., axis=1)` calls a Python function once **per row**: flexible, but a loop in",
        "disguise and slow on big data. Reach for it last. `pd.cut` bins are `(low, high]`: right",
        "edge included."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match each job to the tool.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "one of two values depending on a condition",
          "`np.where`"
        ],
        [
          "translate codes using a dict",
          "`Series.map`"
        ],
        [
          "turn numbers into labelled ranges",
          "`pd.cut`"
        ],
        [
          "arbitrary Python logic per row (slow)",
          "`df.apply(f, axis=1)`"
        ],
        [
          "add columns without changing the original",
          "`df.assign`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Totals with tax",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `add_totals(df, tax_rate)` for a DataFrame with `qty` and `price` columns. Return a",
        "**new** DataFrame (the input must not change) with two extra columns:",
        "",
        "- `net` = `qty * price`",
        "- `gross` = `net * (1 + tax_rate)`, rounded to 2 decimals",
        "",
        "```python",
        "add_totals(df, 0.2)   # net [7.5, 10.0], gross [9.0, 12.0]",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef add_totals(df, tax_rate):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def add_totals(df, tax_rate):",
        "    return df.assign(",
        "        net=df[\"qty\"] * df[\"price\"],",
        "        gross=lambda d: (d[\"net\"] * (1 + tax_rate)).round(2),",
        "    )"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`df.assign(net=..., gross=lambda d: ...)` returns a new frame.",
        "`gross=lambda d: (d[\"net\"] * (1 + tax_rate)).round(2)`"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.DataFrame({\"qty\": [3, 1], \"price\": [2.5, 10.0]})",
        "_out = add_totals(_df, 0.2)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"net\", [7.5, 10.0], _out[\"net\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"gross\", [9.0, 12.0], _out[\"gross\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"the input is unchanged\", [\"qty\", \"price\"], list(_df.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"rounding\", [1.23], add_totals(_pd.DataFrame({\"qty\": [1], \"price\": [1.0]}), 0.2345)[\"gross\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\\.apply\\(",
          "message": "No apply: this is plain arithmetic"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`df` has a million rows. Which is the best way to compute `df[\"a\"] + df[\"b\"]` as a new column?",
      "options": [
        "`df[\"total\"] = df[\"a\"] + df[\"b\"]`",
        "`df[\"total\"] = df.apply(lambda r: r[\"a\"] + r[\"b\"], axis=1)`",
        "a `for` loop over `df.iterrows()`",
        "`df[\"total\"] = [a + b for a, b in zip(df[\"a\"], df[\"b\"])]`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Column arithmetic is one vectorised call. `apply(axis=1)` and `iterrows()` run Python code per row, often 100x slower."
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Label each order as bulk or single.",
      "code": [
        "import numpy as np",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"qty\": [1, 4, 3]})",
        "df[\"kind\"] = np.__1__(df[\"qty\"] __2__ 3, \"bulk\", \"single\")",
        "print(df[\"kind\"].__3__())"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "where",
        ">=",
        "tolist"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "if",
        "select",
        ">",
        "to_list()"
      ],
      "explain": "Prints `['single', 'bulk', 'bulk']`."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Price bands",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `add_band(df)` that returns a new DataFrame with a `band` column built from `price`",
        "with `pd.cut`:",
        "",
        "| price | band |",
        "|---|---|",
        "| 0 < price <= 5 | `cheap` |",
        "| 5 < price <= 20 | `mid` |",
        "| 20 < price <= 1000 | `premium` |",
        "",
        "The tests compare `band` as a list of strings."
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef add_band(df):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def add_band(df):",
        "    return df.assign(band=pd.cut(df[\"price\"], bins=[0, 5, 20, 1000], labels=[\"cheap\", \"mid\", \"premium\"]))"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`bins=[0, 5, 20, 1000]` with three labels.",
        "`df.assign(band=pd.cut(df[\"price\"], bins=..., labels=[...]))`"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.DataFrame({\"price\": [2.5, 5.0, 5.01, 20.0, 99.0]})",
        "_out = add_band(_df)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"bands (right edges included)\", [\"cheap\", \"cheap\", \"mid\", \"mid\", \"premium\"], [str(v) for v in _out[\"band\"].tolist()])",
        "Dojo.check(\"the input is unchanged\", \"band\" not in _df.columns, \"add_band added a column to the original\")"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "pd\\.cut\\(",
          "message": "Uses pd.cut"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Tidy column names",
      "prompt": [
        "Messy files have messy headers. Write `tidy_columns(df)` that returns a new DataFrame where",
        "every column name is stripped of surrounding spaces, lower-cased, and has inner spaces",
        "replaced by `_`; and where the column `notes` (after renaming) is dropped if present.",
        "",
        "```python",
        "# columns: [\" Order ID\", \"Unit Price \", \"QTY\", \"Notes\"]",
        "tidy_columns(df).columns.tolist()   # [\"order_id\", \"unit_price\", \"qty\"]",
        "```",
        "",
        "Column names are a pandas `Index`, which has `.str` methods just like a column of text:",
        "`df.columns.str.strip()`. Use `df.drop(columns=[...], errors=\"ignore\")` to drop a column",
        "that may not exist."
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef tidy_columns(df):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def tidy_columns(df):",
        "    out = df.copy()",
        "    out.columns = out.columns.str.strip().str.lower().str.replace(\" \", \"_\")",
        "    return out.drop(columns=[\"notes\"], errors=\"ignore\")"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`out = df.copy()` then assign `out.columns = ...`.",
        "`out.columns.str.strip().str.lower().str.replace(\" \", \"_\")`, then `drop(columns=[\"notes\"], errors=\"ignore\")`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.DataFrame({\" Order ID\": [1], \"Unit Price \": [2.0], \"QTY\": [3], \"Notes\": [\"x\"]})",
        "Dojo.eq(\"tidied and notes dropped\", [\"order_id\", \"unit_price\", \"qty\"], list(tidy_columns(_df).columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"values kept\", [1, 2.0, 3], tidy_columns(_df).iloc[0].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"the input is unchanged\", [\" Order ID\", \"Unit Price \", \"QTY\", \"Notes\"], list(_df.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"no notes column is fine\", [\"a_b\"], list(tidy_columns(_pd.DataFrame({\"A B\": [1]})).columns))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Enrich the orders",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `enrich(df)` for an orders table with columns `product`, `region`, `qty`, `price`.",
        "Return a new DataFrame with these columns **in this order**:",
        "",
        "`product`, `region_code`, `qty`, `price`, `revenue`, `size`",
        "",
        "- `region_code`: `North` -> `N`, `South` -> `S`, `East` -> `E`, anything else -> `?`",
        "- `revenue`: `qty * price`, rounded to 2 decimals",
        "- `size`: `\"bulk\"` when `qty >= 3`, otherwise `\"single\"`",
        "- the original `region` column is not in the result",
        "",
        "Hint: `.map(codes).fillna(\"?\")` handles regions missing from the dict; select the final",
        "column order with `out[[...]]`."
      ],
      "starter": "import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef enrich(df):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import numpy as np",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "CODES = {\"North\": \"N\", \"South\": \"S\", \"East\": \"E\"}",
        "",
        "",
        "def enrich(df):",
        "    out = df.assign(",
        "        region_code=df[\"region\"].map(CODES).fillna(\"?\"),",
        "        revenue=(df[\"qty\"] * df[\"price\"]).round(2),",
        "        size=np.where(df[\"qty\"] >= 3, \"bulk\", \"single\"),",
        "    )",
        "    return out[[\"product\", \"region_code\", \"qty\", \"price\", \"revenue\", \"size\"]]"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`df[\"region\"].map({\"North\": \"N\", ...}).fillna(\"?\")`",
        "Build everything with `assign`, then `return out[[\"product\", \"region_code\", ...]]`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import io",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.read_csv(io.StringIO('order_id,product,region,qty,price\\n1001,Widget,North,3,2.50\\n1002,Gadget,South,1,10.00\\n1003,Widget,South,5,2.50\\n1004,Gizmo,East,2,7.25\\n1005,Gadget,North,4,10.00\\n1006,Gizmo,North,1,7.25\\n1007,Widget,West,2,2.50\\n'))",
        "_out = enrich(_df)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"columns in order\", [\"product\", \"region_code\", \"qty\", \"price\", \"revenue\", \"size\"], list(_out.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"region codes\", [\"N\", \"S\", \"S\", \"E\", \"N\", \"N\", \"?\"], _out[\"region_code\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"revenue\", [7.5, 10.0, 12.5, 14.5, 40.0, 7.25, 5.0], _out[\"revenue\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"size\", [\"bulk\", \"single\", \"bulk\", \"single\", \"bulk\", \"single\", \"single\"], [str(v) for v in _out[\"size\"].tolist()])",
        "Dojo.check(\"the input still has region\", \"region\" in _df.columns, \"enrich changed its input\")"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\\.apply\\(",
          "message": "No apply"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
